mber\":18,\"labels\":[\"C: target version\"]},{\"type\":\"add_comment\",\"body\":\"Thanks for the report! This is an automated first-pass triage; a maintainer will make the final call.\\n\\n**Reproduction:** Black 26.3.1 and 26.5.1 with `--target-version py314`: not verified. The triage runner's Python is older than 3.14, so Black's safety check could not run (`env_limit`). This is a limit of the runner, not a Black bug.\\n**Assessment:** This looks like deliberate behaviour, not invalid output. PEP 758 (Python 3.14) allows `except A, B:` without parentheses when there is no `as` clause. Black's `remove_parens_around_except_types` feature removes the parentheses for py314 targets (see `future_style.md` in the style docs). Your `SyntaxError` (\\\"multiple exception types must be parenthesized\\\") is what Python 3.13 and earlier raise. Python 3.14 accepts this syntax, so the check may have run on an older interpreter than the one you report.\\n**Next step:** Please run `python3.14 -c \\\"import ast; ast.parse('try:\\\\n    pass\\\\nexcept ValueError, TypeError:\\\\n    pass\\\\n')\\\"` and confirm `python --version`. If it still fails on a real 3.14 interpreter, please share the exact version output. If you want to keep the parentheses, target `py313` or lower.\\n\\n<sub>black-issue-triage skill v1.0.0 · suggested for maintainers: `R: not a bug`</sub>\",\"item_number\":\"18\",\"temporary_id\":\"aw_b7bvwqrM\"}],\"errors\":[]}/tmp/threat-detection-reasons.json","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DHJKaHgqAhj4TF4CdzbKw1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
